  "reason": "The current best (config_039: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, 0.725) has established that multimodal + multiprofile + weighted fusion + transformer aggregation + imagenet_vit_l is the strongest configuration family. The one major untested variable in this family is the RNA encoder: we've shown scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 (~4% gain), but scgpt has never been tested in any multimodal setting. Config_051 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a clean A/B test against config_039, isolating the RNA encoder as the only changed variable. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact remaining design decision: if scgpt outperforms scvi_n200, we get a new best; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 as the superior encoder and can redirect remaining budget to other refinements. Under a limited budget, resolving this single binary question in the context of the current best configuration is more informative than testing lower-priority variants (e.g., concat fusion, which has consistently underperformed weighted)."
}

